{
  "id": "Compound::DB01114 - Gene::6531",
  "verbalization": "Chlorphenamine, a selective antagonist of histamine receptors, is linked to Slc22a2 and Slc6a3 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Chlorphenamine binds to Slc22a2, which is involved in the transport of monoamines across cell membranes. This transporter activity is then associated with Slc6a3, indicating a potential role in dopamine transport. The overlapping pathways suggest that Slc6a3 may be a downstream target of Slc22a2, and that Chlorphenamine may influence its function. The integration of these relationships highlights a possible mechanism by which Chlorphenamine could modulate dopamine transport through Slc6a3, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
